---
layout: layouts/staff.njk
staffPage: resources
staffNum: "05"
staffTitle: Resources
staffHeading: Internal <b>resources</b>
---
{#- NOT `.cards`. That class is a grid of 260px columns, and once the
   shelves went inside it the three SECTIONS became the grid items — so
   Thauma, personal and shared sat side by side in three narrow columns
   instead of stacking, with the cards crushed inside them. Each shelf
   brings its own `.cards` grid; this is just the thing they stack in. -#}
<div id="resourceList"><p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading&hellip;</p></div>
<p class="row-actions"><button class="ghost-btn" id="addResourceBtn" type="button" data-i18n="res.add">+ Add resource</button></p>

{#- A DIALOG, NOT A PANEL AT THE BOTTOM OF THE PAGE.

   It used to be a form below the cards, revealed in place. On a shelf with a
   dozen resources that meant pressing "Add" and having nothing visibly happen
   — the form appeared off-screen, below everything, and the page did not
   move. Editing was worse: the row being edited and the boxes editing it were
   far enough apart to lose track of which resource was open.

   Same `.dlg` shell the confirm dialog uses, so there is one thing on this
   console that means "this is the only thing you are doing right now". -#}
<div class="dlg-back" id="resourceBack" hidden>
  <form class="form dlg" id="resourceForm">
    <h3 id="resourceFormTitle" data-i18n="res.add">Add resource</h3>
    <input type="hidden" id="resourceIndex" value="">
    <input type="text" id="resourceTitle" placeholder="Title" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:res.title" required>
    <textarea id="resourceDescription" placeholder="Description (optional)" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:res.description"></textarea>
    <input type="text" id="resourceLink" placeholder="Link — https://… (optional)" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:res.link">
    <input type="text" id="resourcePhoto" placeholder="Photo URL or /img/… path (optional)" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:res.photo">

    {#- WHO IT IS FOR, and only for somebody who may put something on the
       organization's shelf. A staff member's own resource is governed by
       sharing, so offering them a choice here would be offering a decision
       they are not allowed to make. Hidden rather than disabled: a control
       that cannot be used is noise on the common path. -#}
    <label class="fld" id="resourceWhereRow" hidden>
      <span data-i18n="res.whereLabel">Where it goes</span>
      <select id="resourceWhere">
        <option value="mine" data-i18n="res.whereMine">My resources — private unless I share it</option>
        <option value="staff" data-i18n="res.whereStaff">Thauma resources — every staff member</option>
        <option value="admin" data-i18n="res.whereAdmin">Thauma resources — administrators only</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <div class="dlg-actions">
      <button class="ghost-btn" type="button" id="resourceCancel" data-i18n="common.cancel">Cancel</button>
      <button class="solid-btn" type="submit" data-i18n="res.save">Save resource</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>
<p class="hint" id="saveStatus"></p>
